WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:10.138
Diego Alvarez: Good morning, Cody. Good morning, Hector. How are things in Austin?

2
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:16.430
Cody Barrett: Morning, Diego. Busy as usual. We're in the middle of Q4 push, so every lead counts.

3
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:24.449
Hector Ruiz: Hola, Diego. The Spanish team is doing well. We added two reps last week, so we're up to twelve now.

4
00:00:24.744 --> 00:00:30.624
Diego Alvarez: That's great to hear. How are the call volumes looking across the three states?

5
00:00:31.616 --> 00:00:39.486
Cody Barrett: Steady. We're seeing about 2,400 calls a month from Google Ads and Meta combined. Texas is still the biggest chunk.

6
00:00:40.286 --> 00:00:47.942
Hector Ruiz: And a good portion of those are Spanish speakers. The AI Voice Agent handles the after-hours ones, which helps a lot.

7
00:00:49.126 --> 00:00:54.426
Diego Alvarez: Good. Any issues with the Salesforce sync or the Google Ads conversions lately?

8
00:00:55.764 --> 00:01:04.489
Cody Barrett: No, those are fine. The offline conversions are matching well. But I did want to mention something that came up last week.

9
00:01:05.275 --> 00:01:06.346
Diego Alvarez: Sure, go ahead.

10
00:01:06.586 --> 00:01:18.101
Cody Barrett: We got a pitch from CallRail. They're saying they can sync conversions to Google Ads the same day, and their quote came in noticeably lower than what we're paying now.

11
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.988
Diego Alvarez: Okay. How did that land with your team?

12
00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:32.940
Cody Barrett: It got some attention. Our CFO asked why we're not looking at it. I told him we've got a lot invested in Invoca, but I wanted to flag it.

13
00:01:33.945 --> 00:01:42.557
Hector Ruiz: From my side, the Spanish team relies on the call recordings and the signals. If we switched, we'd lose that history.

14
00:01:43.578 --> 00:01:51.421
Diego Alvarez: I appreciate you telling me. Can you share the quote they sent? I can get our team to look at the comparison.

15
00:01:52.218 --> 00:01:55.117
Cody Barrett: Yeah, I'll forward it after this call.

16
00:01:56.122 --> 00:02:02.240
Diego Alvarez: Thanks. Now, is there anything else on the account side? I saw your usage ticked up in September.

17
00:02:03.024 --> 00:02:08.637
Hector Ruiz: That was probably the Phoenix campaign. We ran a big push there for a week.

18
00:02:09.253 --> 00:02:12.901
Diego Alvarez: Makes sense. And how's the new messaging agent working for follow-ups?

19
00:02:13.429 --> 00:02:18.016
Cody Barrett: It's fine. The team uses it for appointment reminders. No complaints.

20
00:02:19.154 --> 00:02:30.133
Diego Alvarez: Good. I also wanted to check if you need any refresher training on Signal AI Studio. I know you built a few custom signals earlier this year.

21
00:02:30.411 --> 00:02:38.316
Hector Ruiz: We're okay for now. The ones we have are working. Maybe in Q1 we can look at more.

22
00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:47.497
Diego Alvarez: Sounds good. I'll note that. Anything else coming up? I know renewal is a ways off, but just want to keep a pulse.

23
00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:55.091
Cody Barrett: Nothing urgent. We're focused on hitting our Q4 numbers. But that CallRail thing is the main thing on my mind.

24
00:02:55.706 --> 00:03:04.474
Diego Alvarez: Understood. I'll take that back to my team and see what we can do. I'll follow up by early next week.

25
00:03:04.929 --> 00:03:05.979
Cody Barrett: Appreciate it, Diego.

26
00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:08.505
Hector Ruiz: Thanks, Diego. Talk soon.

27
00:03:09.712 --> 00:03:13.405
Diego Alvarez: Thanks, both. Have a good rest of your week.
